Overlay patch, applied by build.sh after the pinned upstream commit is checked out.

What:    TeleopConfig.use_measured_dt: clamp each tick's step by the real elapsed time (capped by
         max_measured_dt) instead of a fixed twist_dt, so a loop that runs slower than its target
         rate does not silently command less than the configured speed. The teleop bridge relies on
         it (its overrun warning says speed "is compensated via use_measured_dt").
Source:  found UNCOMMITTED on opendubs2 (src/mj_manipulator/teleop.py, over 0858fef9912f), captured
         from the 2026-10-09 backup. Who wrote it is not recorded.
Author:  unrecorded -- an uncommitted edit on the robot. MIT, as the upstream repository.
Status:  carried so the image runs what the robot runs. A generic improvement: a candidate for the
         same upstream PR as 0001.
Check:   as 0001.

diff --git a/src/mj_manipulator/teleop.py b/src/mj_manipulator/teleop.py
--- a/src/mj_manipulator/teleop.py
+++ b/src/mj_manipulator/teleop.py
@@ -88,6 +88,27 @@
     """Timestep for twist integration. If None (default), uses
     ctx.control_dt from the execution context. Only set explicitly
     for testing."""
+
+    use_measured_dt: bool = False
+    """If True, use actual wall-clock time since the previous step() call
+    (clamped to max_measured_dt) instead of the fixed twist_dt when
+    computing the per-tick velocity clamp in _check_and_commit/_step_twist.
+
+    twist_dt assumes step() is called at a fixed rate (ctx.control_dt).
+    If the control loop can't sustain that rate (e.g. IK/collision/ROS
+    overhead on a slower CPU), every clamp still limits each step to
+    velocity * twist_dt, but ticks arrive slower than assumed -- so
+    commanded speed silently drops below the configured limit. Measuring
+    real elapsed time fixes that, at the cost of admitting a bigger
+    single-tick step after a stall (still bounded by max_measured_dt).
+    Default False -- preserves existing behavior for callers relying on
+    the fixed-dt assumption."""
+
+    max_measured_dt: float = 0.05
+    """Ceiling on the measured dt used when use_measured_dt is True.
+    Bounds how large a single commanded step can be after a stall (GC
+    pause, ROS hiccup, dropped frame) so a long gap between ticks can't
+    translate into an oversized, potentially unsafe jump."""
 
     idle_timeout: float = 0.5
     """Seconds without input before transitioning to IDLE."""
